{"task_id": "HumanEval/52", "solution": "def below_threshold(l: list, t: int):\n    \"\"\"Return True if all numbers in the list l are below threshold t.\n    >>> below_threshold([1, 2, 4, 10], 100)\n    True\n    >>> below_threshold([1, 20, 4, 10], 5)\n    False\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def validate_inputs(l: list, t: int):\n        \"\"\"Validate input types and element types in the list.\"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(l, list):\n            raise TypeError(\"l must be a list\")\n        if not isinstance(t, int):\n            raise TypeError(\"t must be an int\")\n        for x in l:\n            if not isinstance(x, (int, float)):\n                raise TypeError(f\"All elements in l must be numeric (int or float), got {type(x)}\")\n\n    def compute(l: list, t: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Compute if all elements in l are strictly less than t.\"\"\"\n        for x in l:\n            if not (x < t):\n                return False\n        return True\n\n    validate_inputs(l, t)\n    return compute(l, t)"}
